Third-party references and their licenses
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

s3k/messages.py, s3k/params.py
  The SysEx frame layout, operation codes, and the Program/Keygroup/Sample
  header parameter tables (offsets, field sizes, ranges, and the
  specification's own names for parameters and enumerated values) are
  transcribed as data from Akai's own protocol specifications:

    "S1000 MIDI Exclusive Communication"
      Akai Electric Co. Ltd.
    "S2800/S3000/S3200 MIDI System Exclusive Extensions"
      Akai Electric Co. Ltd.
    "S2000/S3000XL/S3200XL MIDI System Exclusive Extensions"
      Akai Electric Co. Ltd.
      (the source for multi mode: the 0x41/0x42 opcodes and the multi file
      header / multi part field tables)

  None of these documents is redistributed with this project. What is taken from
  them is wire-protocol fact used as data — operation codes, byte offsets,
  field widths, value ranges — which is the minimum needed to interoperate
  with the hardware.

  Two transcription provenance notes that matter for correctness, and are
  repeated at the point of use in the source:

  * The S2800/S3000/S3200 text this project transcribes from is itself a
    hand-typed transcription of a printed Akai document, published at
    <https://lakai.sourceforge.net/docs/s2800_sysex.html>. Its transcriber
    ("Frank") marked points he believed were wrong with "FN" and disclaimed
    any warranty of correctness. Those marks fall in the message-format
    sections, not in the parameter tables — see docs/RESOLUTION_NOTES.md §2
    for exactly where, and what this project does about each.
  * A scan of the S2000/S3000XL/S3200XL document is held by the Internet
    Archive as part of item `S3000XLOM`.

  Everything else here is original work. Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

s3k/bridge.py
  The throttled-output queue (ThrottledOut), the MultiIn merged-input facade,
  the ALSA-client leak fix, and the MIDI port-enumeration helpers are ported
  from the sibling eosed project (eos/bridge.py), which ports them in turn
  from k2kremote (k2kremote/midi_bridge.py), which ports them from:
    mpc2emu (tests/re_banks/krz_sysex_live.py)
    Copyright (C) 2025-2026  mpc2emu contributors
    License: GNU General Public License v2.0 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later)
  All of eosed, k2kremote and mpc2emu are sibling projects by the same
  author, also released under GPL-2.0-or-later. The rest of this file
  (S3kBridge, the autodetect strategy, the config.toml read/write helpers)
  is original work.

All other files (s3k/__init__.py, s3ked/__init__.py, s3ked/app.py,
s3ked/cli.py, s3ked/demo.py, tests/)
  Original work. Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

